# DEFECT 076, the lease's half, found by attacking the string's at the shape
# beside it (M-agreed-retention, 2026-09-23).
#
# `clobber_held` writes over the bytes before the lease it is handed, where the
# lease's block keeps its mark, and `end_lease` then finds the mark gone.
#
# **The line it printed until this case was written was false too.** It said
# *the checker admits `end_lease` only on a lease cell, so this is a compiler
# bug*, and the runtime's own comment above it said the check was *never the
# guard against a program*. Both were measured wrong here: a program reaches it
# on every run, at -O0 and -O2 and under ASan, with a compiler that did nothing
# wrong. The defect was filed with this shape written down as UNRUN; running it
# is what made the class two sites rather than one.
#
# The parameter carries no `lent` on purpose: a lease is a copy C may keep, and
# C keeping it is exactly what lets C write near it.

extern "fixedbugs-c-writes-over-a-leases-header.h"
    function clobber_held(s: cstr)

function main()
    word = repeat("ab", 4)
    x: cstr @ word.lease()
    clobber_held(s: x)
    end_lease(@x)
    print(word)
